# Git commit authorship

When creating commits in this repo (or when asked to commit/PR for Benchmark):

- Author and committer must be **`brentfsienko <brentfsienko@gmail.com>`** — never Cursor, never `*.local` hostname emails.
- Before committing, verify identity if unsure:
  - `git config user.email` should be `brentfsienko@gmail.com`
- If config is wrong for this session, pass identity on the commit command:

```bash
git -c user.name="brentfsienko" -c user.email="brentfsienko@gmail.com" commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
message

EOF
)"
```

- Do not amend already-pushed commits solely to fix authorship unless the user explicitly asks.
- Vercel deploys depend on commits being linked to the GitHub user `brentfsienko`.
